 "problems": [
  "Six Wikipedia fetches returned URL_NOT_FOUND (listed in pages_failed); the Transcaspian government dossier cites an alternative page, the other five states were dropped or written from sibling pages.",
  "Date conflicts followed one page and recorded the loser in notes: Tashkent end 1809 (not 1808/1807); Kandahar end 1855/11 (not Sept 1856); Herat start 1818 (page also gives 1793/1801); Khalkha end 1688 (not 1691/1696); Turkestan Autonomy Nov 1917 (not Feb 1918).",
  "kingdom-of-afghanistan (ia-03-f) lacks 1929 losses for Ghazni and Mazar-i Sharif that emirate-of-afghanistan-1929 supports.",
  "qing-dynasty, republic-of-china (ea-08), ottoman-empire (me-10) and russian-empire (eu-17) need matching events for kumul-khanate, yettishar, ili-sultanate (Russian occupation 1871 to 1883/3) and first-east-turkestan-republic; no qing-dynasty dossier existed on 2026-10-19.",
  "kazakh-khanate (ia-03-a) names Tashkent as tashkent-state-of-yunus-khoja; this batch uses tashkent-state (the khanate-of-kokand slug).",
  "The 1924 Uzbek, Turkmen, Tajik, Kara-Kirghiz and Karakalpak units have no dossiers, so successors of the Soviet-era Central Asian dossiers point to union-of-soviet-socialist-republics.",
  "Only validator warning: khanate-of-kalat is an unknown slug in principality-of-kandahar (2 vassal events).",
  "khalkha-khanates supplies the corrected shape for 15 Golden Horde rows (1636-1695) that golden-horde (ia-02-x) marks wrong."
 ]
}